+# Hegel property-based testing report — `quinn-proto`
+
+Tests were added with the `hegeltest` crate (library name `hegel`) following the
+hegel skill workflow. All work is confined to `quinn-proto`. Property tests were
+added to the existing test module of the code they exercise (never a new file).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+| # | Property | Test (module::name) | Evidence |
+|---|----------|---------------------|----------|
+| 1 | `decode(encode(x)) == x` for every representable `VarInt`; the encoding is exactly `size()` bytes and decode consumes all of it | `varint::tests::varint_encode_decode_roundtrip` | `Codec` trait doc ("infallible encoding and decoding"), `VarInt::size()`, RFC 9000 §16; generalizes the hardcoded `check_pn`-style cases |
+| 2 | `VarInt::decode` never panics on arbitrary bytes; any decoded value is `<= MAX` and value-roundtrips | `varint::tests::varint_decode_arbitrary_bytes` | `VarInt` doc "integer less than 2^62"; varints are parsed from untrusted network data |
+| 3 | Any `PacketNumber` of any width wire-roundtrips; encoding is `len()` bytes and `decode_len(tag) == len()` | `packet::tests::pn_wire_roundtrip` | generalizes `roundtrip_packet_numbers` unit test |
+| 4 | RFC 9000 App. A: `PacketNumber::new(n, largest_acked).expand(expected) == n` for any decoder reference `expected` in `[largest_acked, n]` | `packet::tests::pn_new_expand_recovers_original` | generalizes exhaustive small-range `pn_expand_roundtrip` to the full 2^62 packet-number space |
+| 5 | `PartialDecode::new` never panics; on success every input byte is accounted for once between the packet and trailing bytes | `packet::tests::partial_decode_accounts_for_every_byte` | direct port of `fuzz/fuzz_targets/packet.rs` |
+| 6 | Any valid `TransportParameters`, in any serialization order and with any grease parameter, decodes back identically | `transport_parameters::test::params_write_read_roundtrip` | generalizes the `coding` unit test; `fuzz/fuzz_targets/params.rs`; value ranges follow the semantic-validation rules in `read` |
+| 7 | `TransportParameters::read` never panics on garbage or mutated-valid encodings, for either side | `transport_parameters::test::params_read_never_panics` | direct port of `fuzz/fuzz_targets/params.rs` |
+| 8 | Any non-empty ACK range set + delay + ECN counts encode to one ACK frame that decodes to the same ranges/delay/counts | `frame::test::ack_roundtrip` | generalizes the `ack_coding` unit test |
+| 9 | The frame `Iter` never panics on arbitrary payload bytes | `frame::test::frame_iter_never_panics` | frame payloads are decrypted network data; parse-robustness |
+| 10 | CID retirement protocol: retirement ranges are non-empty, no sequence retired twice, active seq never decreases nor equals a retired seq, `active()` never panics | `cid_queue::tests::retirement::cid_queue_retires_each_sequence_at_most_once` (stateful) | doc comments on `insert`/`next`, RFC 9000 §5.1.2 |
+| 11 | `StreamId::new(side, dir, index)` returns those three components and roundtrips through `VarInt` | `tests::stream_id_roundtrip` | port of `fuzz/fuzz_targets/streamid.rs`, extended with the accessor docs and the `Codec`/`VarInt` conversions |
+| 12 | Payload written in arbitrary chunks over a simulated link (arbitrary MTU ≥ 1200, arbitrary latency) is delivered exactly and in order | `tests::stream_data_integrity_across_simulated_link` | built on the crate's own `Pair` harness and the `finish_stream_simple` stream API |
+| 13 | `RangeSet` and `ArrayRangeSet` agree with a `BTreeSet<u64>` element model after every insert/remove/replace/pop_min/contains, incl. len/min/max/is_empty summaries | `range_set::tests::model::range_sets_match_element_model` (stateful model test) | mirrors `RefRangeSet` and the `compare_*_to_reference` unit tests; the two production sets must be behaviourally identical |
+| 14 | `RangeSet::replace(x..x)` (empty range) leaves an empty set empty — **documents a real bug (fails)** | `range_set::btree_range_set::tests::replace_empty_range_corrupts_set` | the empty-range guards in `insert`/`remove`, and the `RangeSet` "never holds empty ranges" invariant |
